.TH "FLOX" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox \- developer environments you can take with you
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general options>] <command>
     [<command options>]
     [<args>] ...
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Flox is a virtual environment and package manager all in one.
.PP
With Flox you create environments that layer and provide dependencies
just where it matters, making them portable across the full software
lifecycle.
.SS Command Line Completions
Flox ships with command line completions for \f[CR]bash\f[R],
\f[CR]fish\f[R] and \f[CR]zsh\f[R].
These completions are installed alongside Flox.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-h\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Prints help information.
.PP
The following options can be passed when running any \f[CR]flox\f[R]
subcommand but must be specified \f[I]before\f[R] the subcommand.
.TP
\f[CR]\-v\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase logging verbosity.
Invoke multiple times for increasing detail.
.TP
\f[CR]\-q\f[R], \f[CR]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Silence logs except for errors.
.SS Flox Options
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-version\f[R]
Print \f[CR]flox\f[R] version.
.SH COMMANDS
Flox commands are grouped into categories pertaining to local
development, sharing environments, and administration.
.SS Local Development Commands
.TP
\f[CR]init\f[R]
Create an environment in the current directory.
.TP
\f[CR]activate\f[R]
Enter the environment, run \f[CR]flox deactivate\f[R] to leave.
.TP
\f[CR]deactivate\f[R]
Deactivate the current environment.
.TP
\f[CR]search\f[R]
Search for system or library packages to install.
.TP
\f[CR]show\f[R]
Show details about a single package.
.TP
\f[CR]install\f[R], \f[CR]i\f[R]
Install packages into an environment.
.TP
\f[CR]uninstall\f[R]
Uninstall installed packages from an environment.
.TP
\f[CR]edit\f[R]
Edit the declarative environment configuration file.
.TP
\f[CR]list\f[R], \f[CR]l\f[R]
List packages installed in an environment.
.TP
\f[CR]delete\f[R]
Delete an environment.
.SS Sharing Commands
.TP
\f[CR]push\f[R]
Send an environment to FloxHub.
.TP
\f[CR]pull\f[R]
Pull an environment from FloxHub.
.SS Additional Commands
.TP
\f[CR]update\f[R]
Update an environment\(cqs base catalog or update the global base
catalog.
.TP
\f[CR]upgrade\f[R]
Upgrade packages in an environment.
.TP
\f[CR]config\f[R]
View and set configuration options.
.TP
\f[CR]auth\f[R]
FloxHub authentication commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
\f[CR]$FLOX_DISABLE_METRICS\f[R]
Variable for disabling the collection/sending of metrics data.
If set to \f[CR]true\f[R], prevents Flox from submitting basic metrics
information such as a unique token and the subcommand issued.
.TP
\f[CR]$FLOX_MAX_PARALLEL_DOWNLOADS\f[R]
Variable for controlling parallel downloads when building an
environment.
By default, every package for an environment is downloaded in parallel,
but on poor connections this can cause packages to download slower and
in some cases time out.
Setting this to a number greater than or equal to 1 will limit the
number of active downloads to the specified number.
.TP
\f[CR]$EDITOR\f[R], \f[CR]$VISUAL\f[R]
Override the default editor used for editing environment manifests and
commit messages.
.TP
\f[CR]$SSL_CERT_FILE\f[R], \f[CR]$NIX_SSL_CERT_FILE\f[R]
If set, overrides the path to the default Flox provided SSL certificate
bundle.
Set \f[CR]NIX_SSL_CERT_FILE\f[R] to only override packages built with
Nix, and otherwise set \f[CR]SSL_CERT_FILE\f[R] to override the value
for all packages.
.RS
.PP
See also: \f[B]Nix environment variables \-
\f[CB]NIX_SSL_CERT_FILE\f[B]\f[R] <\f[I]https://nixos.org/manual/nix/stable/installation/env\-variables.html#nix_ssl_cert_file\f[R]>
.RE
